<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!-- What a camp's people build with, by their age (Source/ColonyCouncil/Camps/CampKit.cs, laid out by CampBuildMath.cs):
       for each role the player's mods' pieces first (MayRequire, picked from the active rows of docs/player-mods/buildings.tsv
       for the role and the age), the game's own last, which is always there. The first that exists and that the people
       know how to build (its research within their age) is used, of the first listed material it can be made of.
       Roles: fire; bed (a bed each); tent (a tent that is a bed, for the kinds that sleep in tents); hut and door (a hut's
       walls and door); tentwall and tentdoor (a tent's, when no tent is a bed); wall (a windbreak); table and seat; light;
       butcher and craft (their work spots); stall (a trader's table); picket (where pack beasts are tied); stash (a shelf
       for their goods, for a stay of a day and a half or more, only one the game keeps things on without them
       deteriorating: CampKit.Keeps; a people who know none, a tribe, put up a store tent of their tentwall and tentdoor
       instead: Camps/CampStore.cs).
       Grows: what a camp of the age adds over its stay (Source/ColonyCouncil/Camps/CampGrow.cs, CampBuildMath.GrowWants), the
       player's mods' pieces first, from the active rows of docs/player-mods; a role with no piece that exists and that the
       people know how to build is simply not added (there is no game piece for a drying rack, a firewood rack, a banner, a
       latrine or a food basket). post (a lean-to's posts over the stash: VFE Settlers' post, else a column); fence (a pen
       for their beasts: VFE Architect's picket fence, else the game's fence); drying (VFE Classical's meat drying rack, for
       hunters); stonework and tailoring (a bench for their trade); woodpile (Deep Storage Plus's firewood rack, for
       woodcutters, of the logs they cut); shrine (Ideology's small altar, for a people of a faith); banner (VFE Medieval 2's
       heraldic standing banner) and imperialbanner (VFE Empire's, for the Empire's people); latrine (Dubs Bad Hygiene's pit
       latrine); basket (LWM's Deep Storage food basket, a second store for their food). Seats round the fire are the kit's
       seat, a second store for other goods the kit's stash. -->

